    "question": {
      ":question/id": "668737d9-e31a-5d02-a405-d85ea707a663",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the line integral of $f(x,y)=- \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}$ along the curve\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 2 t^{2},- 2 t^{2}\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le \\sqrt{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}.\n$$\n\nGive the exact value.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s &=\\int_a^b f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{r}(t)=(2 t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{i}+(- 2 t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{j}$, then along the curve we have $x=2 t^{2}$, $y=- 2 t^{2}$.\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}'(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2 t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 2 t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(4 t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(- 4 t)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4 t)^2+(- 4 t)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{32 t^{2}} \\\\  & =4 \\sqrt{2}|t| \\\\  & =4 \\sqrt{2} t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $|t|=t$ because $t\\geq0$ along the path of $C.$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=- \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =- \\cos{\\left(2 t^{2} \\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}}f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{\\frac{\\pi}{6}}}(- \\cos{\\left(2 t^{2} \\right)})(4 \\sqrt{2} t)\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=2 t^{2}$, $\\text{d}u=(4 t)\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}}- \\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\cos u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =- \\sqrt{2}\\sin u\\big|_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{3}} \\\\  & =- \\sqrt{2}[\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)-\\sin(0)] \\\\  & =- \\sqrt{2}[\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)-(0)] \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\right)-(0) \\\\  & =- \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "3de6573b-6945-5d62-8fe8-668b48294eeb",
