    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7099a7db-564b-561b-8dad-78cf76ad3f20",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the line integral of $f(x,y)=x^{3} + 3 y$ along the curve\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle 3 t,t^{3}\\rangle,\\qquad 0\\le t\\le \\sqrt[4]{2}.\n$$\n\nGive the exact value.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s &=\\int_a^b f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{r}(t)=(3 t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(t^{3})\\,\\mathbf{j}$, then along the curve we have $x=3 t$, $y=t^{3}$.\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}'(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3 t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{3})\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =(3)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(3 t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3)^2+(3 t^{2})^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9 t^{4} + 9} \\\\  & =3 \\sqrt{t^{4} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x^{3} + 3 y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =(3 t)^3+(3)(t^{3}) \\\\  & =27t^3+3t^3 \\\\  & =30 t^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[4]{2}}f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[4]{2}}(30 t^{3})(3 \\sqrt{t^{4} + 1})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[4]{2}}90 t^{3} \\sqrt{t^{4} + 1}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=t^{4} + 1$, $\\text{d}u=(4 t^{3})\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{45}{2}\\cdot u^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{2}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\big|_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =15[(3)^{3/2}-(1)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =15[(3 \\sqrt{3})-(1)] \\\\  & =(45 \\sqrt{3})-(15) \\\\  & =-15 + 45 \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
